# The sheet copies the household's own recordings next to itself so a browser
# can play them, and the downloaded annotations are one person's judgements
# about their family's afternoon. Neither belongs in the repository.
# make_graphrag_slice.py rebuilds the sheet from the frozen items file at any
# time, and slice.*.items.json IS tracked, because the population a retrieval
# score is computed over has to stay auditable: it carries times, rooms and
# event ids, and no speech.
sheets/
graphrag_slice_*.json

# Measurements, regenerated by re-running the tools over the annotations.
graphrag_negative_probes.json
graphrag_retrieval.*.json
graphrag_retrieval.*.tsv

__pycache__/

# Lists written for a resident to judge, and what they wrote back. The
# transcript in them is the household speaking.
disputes_*.txt

# The answers GraphRag gave about the household, quarrel by quarrel: data, not code.
graphrag_incident_eval*.json
